From 0a01e50c1832f3d19ffe4bd7d55224136b67359b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:37:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/27] victory-formats: Layout::copy_table, the detile's runs
 as data

The runs `Layout::detile` copies for one subresource, as a table for
another copier (a compute shader): the column runs once, the rows once
(tiled base, XOR bits, linear offset), so `runs + rows` entries rather
than their product (BC7 4096x4096, whole chain: 4,098). `apply` is the
CPU reference of the copy, bounds-checked; `aligned(4)` says whether a
32-bit-word copier can take it. `walk` is left as it was.

Tests: byte-for-byte parity with `detile` (padding included) over every
layout family at odd and 256-byte pitches, the same refusals, alignment,
and the table sizes of 1K-4K BC7 textures.

(cherry picked from commit d8a3df88f36eb48037671c3bd067426306736758)
---
 crates/victory-formats/src/texture.rs | 361 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 361 insertions(+)

